-- title:
--   Finite query program with exact terminal and singleton branches
-- statement:
--   This fixed 510-instruction program reads the persistent terminal state and one real query $q$. It finds the earliest closest terminal, returns a stored image exactly on a terminal query, and otherwise computes the correlation data from the available distances. The fixed projected subgradient solver supplies $w$, and the output is
--
--   $$F(q)=(b_k+\rho w,\rho\sqrt{1-\|w\|^2}),\qquad\rho=\|q-x_k\|.$$
--
--   For one terminal the program outputs $\|q-x_1\|$ in one coordinate. It never changes the stored terminal coordinates, images, distances or header. Query points may lie anywhere in the ambient real Euclidean space, including outside the terminal span. Each operation and every iteration is charged by the common machine semantics.
-- source:
--   Vladimir Braverman, Kuan Cheng, Jiaqing Zhu, STOC 2027 submission #1373 (October 2026), pp. 18–22, equations (33), (36), (40)–(41), query bound (49); https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1373.pdf

